                    'attributed to XPENG. Researched to company filings, exchange releases, OICA, the IFR and named '
                    'research houses. || ✅ THE MUSK QUOTE IS REAL AND RECENT. G20 Innovation Ministerial, Chapel Hill, '
                    '1 SEPTEMBER 2026, by video: "Ten years from now, I would say there are well over a billion '
                    'humanoid robots" and "The productivity per robot will be probably five times that of a human." IT '
                    'IS A CUMULATIVE INSTALLED BASE BY ABOUT 2036, NOT AN ANNUAL RATE. || ⚠️ BUT MUSK HAS GIVEN AT '
                    'LEAST SIX DIFFERENT VERSIONS AND THEY CONTRADICT EACH OTHER BY TWENTY TIMES. January 2024 on X he '
                    'AGREED WITH SOMEONE ELSE\'S number - "a billion humanoid robots on earth in the 2040s" - replying '
                    '"Probably something like that." At the 13 JUNE 2024 shareholder meeting he said BOTH "the baud '
                    'rate will be probably something ultimately, like a billion A YEAR humanoid robots" AND "there\'ll '
                    'be more than 10 billion humanoid robots in the world, probably 20 or more" - IN THE SAME SITTING. '
                    'October 2024 in Riyadh it was 10 billion by 2040. NOW IT IS ONE BILLION BY 2036. A forecast that '
                    'moves between 1 billion and 20 billion, and between cumulative and annual, is a mood rather than '
                    'a plan. || 📊 THE ARITHMETIC NOBODY ON THE SLIDE DID. ONE BILLION OVER TEN YEARS IS AN AVERAGE OF '
                    'ONE HUNDRED MILLION UNITS A YEAR. GLOBAL MOTOR VEHICLE PRODUCTION IN 2025 WAS 96.4 MILLION UNITS '
                    '(OICA, published 23 April 2026). SO THE CLAIM REQUIRES BUILDING MORE HUMANOID ROBOTS EVERY YEAR '
                    'THAN THE ENTIRE WORLD BUILDS CARS - FROM A STANDING START, WITH A SUPPLY CHAIN THAT DOES NOT '
                    'EXIST. Measured against the closest real analogue it is worse: THE ENTIRE GLOBAL INSTALLED BASE '
                    'OF INDUSTRIAL ROBOTS, ACCUMULATED OVER ABOUT SIXTY YEARS, IS 4,664,000 UNITS, with 542,000 '
                    'installed in 2024 (IFR World Robotics 2025). ONE BILLION IS 214 TIMES THE INSTALLED BASE AND THE '
                    'REQUIRED RUN-RATE IS 185 TIMES CURRENT ANNUAL INSTALLATIONS. || ⚠️⚠️ AND EVEN THE MOST BULLISH '
                    'MAINSTREAM FORECAST IS FOURTEEN YEARS BEHIND HIM. MORGAN STANLEY (Adam Jonas and Sheng Zhong, 14 '
                    'May 2025) reaches ONE BILLION CUMULATIVE IN 2050, not 2036, and says explicitly: "Adoption should '
                    'be relatively slow until the mid-2030s, accelerating in the late 2030s and 2040s." INTERACT '
                    'ANALYSIS (19 May 2026) forecasts ABOUT 700,000 UNITS A YEAR IN 2035 - which is 0.7% OF THE '
                    'HUNDRED-MILLION RUN-RATE THE CLAIM NEEDS. The forecasters also disagree violently with each '
                    'other: Berg Insight says 16,000 units in 2026 while Counterpoint MEASURED over 22,000 IN THE '
                    'FIRST HALF ALONE. || ⚠️⚠️⚠️ THE DECIDING EVIDENCE IS THE TRACK RECORD, AND IT IS NOT CLOSE. TESLA '
                    'AUTONOMY DAY, APRIL 2019: "over a million robotaxis on the road" BY 2020. ACTUAL, FROM TEXAS DMV '
                    'REGISTRATION DATA ON 2 JUNE 2026: FORTY-TWO REGISTERED ROBOTAXIS. THAT IS A MISS OF ROUGHLY '
                    'TWENTY-FOUR THOUSAND TIMES. CYBERTRUCK: "roughly a quarter-million Cybertrucks a year" promised, '
                    'ABOUT 17,012 DELIVERED IN FULL-YEAR 2025 - 93% SHORT, AND SPACEX ITSELF BOUGHT 1,279 OF THEM IN '
                    'Q4. TESLA SEMI: production promised for 2019 at the November 2017 unveiling, SERIAL PRODUCTION '
                    'BEGAN 29 APRIL 2026 - SEVEN YEARS LATE. ROADSTER 2.0: unveiled November 2017 for 2020 production, '
                    'STILL NOT IN PRODUCTION NINE YEARS ON, with 50,000-dollar deposits held since 2017. FULL '
                    'SELF-DRIVING HAS BEEN "later this year" FOR TEN CONSECUTIVE YEARS. AND OPTIMUS ITSELF: Musk said '
                    'on 30 January 2025 the plan called for "roughly 10,000 Optimus robots to be built this year" and '
                    'publicly pledged at least 5,000 - THE INFORMATION REPORTED THE ACTUAL NUMBER WAS "ONLY IN THE '
                    'HUNDREDS". ⚠️ NO COUNTER-EXAMPLE WAS FOUND IN THIS RESEARCH WHERE A MUSK PRODUCTION-VOLUME '
                    "FORECAST WAS MET ON THE STATED DATE. || ⚠️ AND TESLA'S OWN FILINGS ARE QUIETER THAN ITS FOUNDER. "
                    'THE Q2 2026 FORM 10-Q DOES NOT CONTAIN THE WORDS "OPTIMUS" OR "HUMANOID" AT ALL. The FY2025 10-K '
                    'calls it "a general purpose, autonomous humanoid robot IN DEVELOPMENT" in "a nascent industry '
                    'that has yet to develop commercially". TESLA HAS NEVER PUBLISHED AN OPTIMUS UNIT COUNT IN ANY SEC '
                    'FILING. On the Q1 2026 call Musk said, verbatim: "I DON\'T KNOW WHAT THE PRODUCTION RATE OF '
                    'OPTIMUS WILL BE THIS YEAR. IT IS IMPOSSIBLE TO PREDICT THESE THINGS," and that it "will move as '
                    'fast as the least lucky, slowest, dumbest part in the entire 10,000". The Gen 3 reveal promised '
                    'for Q1 2026 slipped to "middle of this year" and AS OF 16 SEPTEMBER HAS STILL NOT HAPPENED. || '
                    '⚠️⚠️ NOW THE SECOND SLIDE, AND IT IS WRONG ON THE COMPANY AND MISLEADING ON THE NUMBER. THE '
                    "FACTORY IS NOT XPENG'S. IT IS UBTECH ROBOTICS (HKEX 9880) AT LIUZHOU, GUANGXI, COMMISSIONED 12 "
