                    'basis 2.67% is right, while the minus 8.3% I quoted is one quarter distorted by the CyberArk '
                    'acquisition. || 💡 THE LESSON IS THE ONE THIS BOARD KEEPS RELEARNING FROM THE OTHER DIRECTION: '
                    'BEFORE CALLING A FIELD WRONG, CHECK WHAT PERIOD IT IS MEASURING. I have spent this week demanding '
                    'that every research figure carry its period and its definition, and then failed to apply the same '
                    'test to my own board. The correct way to have phrased it yesterday was: "the board carries the '
                    'FULL-YEAR margin of 2.67%, and the LATEST QUARTER was minus 8.3% - the gap is acquisition '
                    'accounting." That is the same information without a false alarm. || ⚠️ A FALSE ALARM IS NOT '
                    'HARMLESS. It is the same fault I flagged in my own sweep yesterday when it wrongly called Intel '
                    'over-scheduled: A TEST THAT CRIES WOLF IS WORSE THAN NO TEST, BECAUSE THE NEXT REAL WARNING GETS '
                    'IGNORED. Two false positives from me in two days is a pattern, and the fix is the same as for the '
                    'board itself: STATE THE PERIOD AND THE DEFINITION BEFORE STATING THE VERDICT. || FOR '
                    'COMPLETENESS, THE PANW FIELDS AS THEY NOW STAND AND WHAT THEY MEASURE: revenue 11.48 billion is '
                    'FISCAL 2026, ended 31 July 2026. Net margin 2.67% is that same year. Revenue growth of 24.5% is '
